Subject: precon_search finds a precon by its set's name and names the set

Found in the assistant tool review of the live gateway (2026-10-28): set
names were not searchable ("Reality Fracture" found nothing while "FRC"
worked) and the results did not say the set. precon_search now reads
MTGJSON's SetList.json (the service DeckList.json comes from, no new host),
kept a day, and matches the query against the deck's name, the set code and
the set's name, as typed or word by word in any order ("warhammer 40000"
finds the Warhammer 40,000 Commander decks). Each result names its set.
When the set list can't be read, the search works as before on names and
codes.

tests/test_precon_search_set_names.py; tests/test_research_wording.py's
precon test gets the set list from a fake too.

Upstream: Kautiontape/mystic-forge at dd82cd1 has none of these. Needs
patches 0001-0017 applied first.
